# CODEOWNERS — who reviews what.
#
# GitHub reads this file to decide whose review a pull request requests. It takes effect
# only when branch protection requires a code-owner review (`Require review from Code
# Owners`); until that setting is on, this file states the intent and asks for nothing.
#
# TWO RULES FOR THIS FILE:
#
#   1. PUBLIC GITHUB HANDLES ONLY. A handle is how a reviewer is addressed in the open;
#      a person's name, an address or a phone number is the operator's private data and
#      never belongs in a public repository (RULES/04). A handle is written `@handle`,
#      a team `@org/team-name` — never a name.
#   2. ROLES REVIEW, NOT PEOPLE. The paths below are grouped by what the code does, so a
#      fleet with more than one maintainer can put a different handle on each line and a
#      fleet of one keeps the default.
#
# A later pattern wins over an earlier one. Keep the catch-all first.

# ── the default: every change needs a maintainer's review ────────────────────────────────────
*                                   @zerwiz

# ── the law and its gates: the rules, the wards, the delivery gate ───────────────────────────
/RULES/                             @zerwiz
/bin/gates/                         @zerwiz
/.github/                           @zerwiz

# ── the runtime: what a stranger's install runs ─────────────────────────────────────────────
/bin/engine/                        @zerwiz
/src/ymir_runtime/                  @zerwiz
/bin/seat/                          @zerwiz
/bin/agents/                        @zerwiz

# ── the apps: each has a window, and each is reviewed by its own owner when one is named ────
/apps/                              @zerwiz

# ── the records: plans, features, fix notes — the documents a person reads ──────────────────
/docs/                              @zerwiz
/FEATURES.md                        @zerwiz

# ── a second maintainer's areas, as a shape to copy ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Put a handle on the line, never a name. For example, if a maintainer takes the apps:
#
#   /apps/                            @another-public-handle
